+
+### ECON-02B2d6 — NPC construction crews (Linux local prototype)
+
+The colony interface can now assign named resident NPCs to authorized structural plans.
+The main C++ colony process advances workers over a persistent local grid,
+respects installed walls/doors, accumulates labor and consumes real manufactured
+modules through the existing structural construction command. Crew assignments,
+positions, pause/resume state and progress survive SQLite restart. This is
+site-local work, **not yet material hauling, 3D agent movement, or cross-site
+NPC travel**. See `docs/engineering/ECON02B2d6_NPC_Construction_Crews_2026-11-01.md`.
+
+Verify the new milestone with:
+
+```sh
+ctest --test-dir build -R 'ECON02B2d6_' --output-on-failure
+python3 scripts/colony_crew_browser_smoke.py
+```
